WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:07.970
They say one little leak can sink a massive
ship - massive ship - can completely sink

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.180
because of one little leak.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:14.990
By the way, your business, your enterprise,
you as an entrepreneur, you can absolutely

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:18.600
sink your ship if you don't plug the little
leaks you have in your business.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:23.619
And today, I'm going to talk to you about
three different companies, from three different

00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:29.080
industries, if I'm running them, how I'm going
to find those leaks and how I would plug them.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:33.860
I wish we had hours and hours together to
go through your business, but whatever I'm

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:37.540
talking about here today, I'm going to give
you feedback on what you need to do at the

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:38.540
end with your business.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:44.010
So, the first thing I do is whenever I'm running
any business, and we have an area that's not

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.010
going well.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.010
Like today we just had a conference call.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:49.590
It was a pretty strong conference call I had
with everybody, and we went through areas

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.720
that we need to be improving in.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.590
First thing I do is I write out all the steps.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:57.440
And I do this with every aspect of my life
and my business.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.739
For instance, if it's health, I write out
every single thing I do with my diet and every

00:01:02.739 --> 00:01:08.140
single routine I have with working out, and
every single routine I have with sleep, everything.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:12.000
So step #1 is take out your business and write
all the steps.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.660
It could be 20 steps.

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:15.310
It could be 10 steps.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:19.090
Customer comes in, what they do next and what
they do . . . until they buy from you.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:20.549
All the steps.

00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:25.210
Once you write all the steps, prioritize the
five most important steps.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:29.530
So go this is the most important step, then
this, then this, then this.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:33.810
Then rank how well you do in each step.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:39.430
Then bring a group of two, three, four, five
people that work with you that are also leaders,

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:42.190
who can say, I think we can do this to improve.

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:43.580
I think we can do this to improve this.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.030
We're not doing this that well.

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:47.800
Then put an action plan together and attack
the action plan.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:51.909
So whatever I just told you right now, watch
how I do this with these different businesses.

00:01:51.909 --> 00:01:55.729
I've got a sales office, any sales office,
real estate, insurance, it doesn't matter

00:01:55.729 --> 00:01:57.130
what it is, sales office.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:00.150
We've got a restaurant here, and then we have
a construction business here.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:01.350
Let's start here with sales office.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.370
I'm running a sales office.

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:06.530
Real estate, pharmaceuticals sales, whatever
it is.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:09.979
I want to find out where my leaks in my business
are.

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:16.139
So I either have inbound calls or customers
coming in, or I have outbound calls, reaching

00:02:16.139 --> 00:02:17.139
out.

00:02:17.139 --> 00:02:18.700
I'm reaching out or I'm getting the call.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.569
I'm getting an email of interest.

00:02:20.569 --> 00:02:22.239
I'm getting a message.

00:02:22.239 --> 00:02:25.510
I'm getting a visit to my business, whatever
it is.

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:26.939
Or I'm outbound.

00:02:26.939 --> 00:02:31.529
So if I'm inbound call, somebody calls me,
yes, I would like to talk to a real estate

00:02:31.529 --> 00:02:33.560
agent about buying a house, hypothetically.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:34.599
What is my script?

00:02:34.599 --> 00:02:36.650
I test the script.

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:38.099
What is the questions asked?

00:02:38.099 --> 00:02:41.860
What questions are we asking, the sales rep
is asking the customer that's called in.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.120
Three, what are my FAQs?

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.690
Do I have an FAQ sheet.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:50.629
For instance, If you're running real estate,
there are 20 questions that everybody's going

00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:52.659
to ask.

00:02:52.659 --> 00:02:57.099
Everybody that buys a house asks the same
exact questions.

00:02:57.099 --> 00:03:00.120
Everybody that's selling and buying asks the
same exact questions.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:01.709
So I need an FAQ sheet.

00:03:01.709 --> 00:03:03.299
Do I have an FAQ sheet?

00:03:03.299 --> 00:03:05.650
Next thing is called call to action.

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:07.629
So let's just say a person calls, I have a
script.

00:03:07.629 --> 00:03:12.150
And I ask questions, they ask me questions,
I already know the FAQs.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:13.309
Then it's call to action.

00:03:13.309 --> 00:03:15.549
Meaning, "when do you want to buy the house?

00:03:15.549 --> 00:03:17.010
How soon do you want to buy the house?

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.010
Are you already prequalified?

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:19.299
Do you already have a property?

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:20.790
Do you already know what area?"

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:23.729
I'm asking, call to action, what do we do
next.

00:03:23.729 --> 00:03:24.729
Then we're going to go.

00:03:24.729 --> 00:03:26.800
Schedule a time to go do whatever we're doing.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:27.930
And then we're going to close.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:31.450
And when I close, then it's follow up, once
I got the close.

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:33.019
Then I follow up as we got closed.

00:03:33.019 --> 00:03:37.249
Then there's onboarding, paperwork, all this
stuff, filling out all these things I've got

00:03:37.249 --> 00:03:38.249
to do.

00:03:38.249 --> 00:03:41.060
Then it's referral, then it's nurturing that
relationship.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:45.359
If it's outbound, and I'm reaching out to
the customer.

00:03:45.359 --> 00:03:49.599
Let's just say I am a social media marketing
company and I'm running an agency and I'm

00:03:49.599 --> 00:03:50.599
outbound.

00:03:50.599 --> 00:03:52.029
I'm trying to reach out to people.

00:03:52.029 --> 00:03:54.030
First I have to identify who my ideal client
is.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:56.439
Do I even know who my ideal client is to call?

00:03:56.439 --> 00:04:04.299
Then it's volume of contacts, meaning if I'm
selling a membership to a magazine, it's volume.

00:04:04.299 --> 00:04:09.230
If I'm selling a subscription to a certain
membership or whatever, it's volume.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.019
If I'm selling a gym membership, it's volume.

00:04:11.019 --> 00:04:12.459
I'm calling everybody.

00:04:12.459 --> 00:04:19.190
But if I'm selling exotic cars, Lamborghinis,
Ferraris, I'm not contacting 200 people in

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:20.190
a day.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:22.940
I'm nurturing, meaning I'm going to country
club events.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:25.530
I'm going to certain speaking events.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:29.250
I'm going to certain places that people of
money are going to be around.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:32.910
So volume is quantity vs. quality, depending
on the product that you sell.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.350
You need to be clear about that.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.380
Then, am I good at finding customers?

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:37.590
Some companies have finding problems.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.780
They don't know how to find the right customers.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.870
Then what's my script, when I'm outbound.

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:43.380
Closing, do I close well?

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.450
Do I have a finding or closing problem?

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.550
Follow up, onboarding, nurture, all the same.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:52.790
So now, once I know what my inbound and outbound
is, and I write this out.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:54.240
Let's just say this is you.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.080
I'm going to circle the most important ones
on inbound.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.280
For instance, FAQs.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.400
That's important for everybody to know the
FAQs.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.170
Great, that's important.

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:05.280
Questions asked is important.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.680
Close is important.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.890
And man, follow up has to be up there.

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:11.180
Then I'm going to score every one of them
how well we do.

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:12.180
Our script sucks, man.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:13.180
We're at two.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:15.370
We don't even have a script, honestly.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:18.560
Two, questions asked, we don't even know what
questions to ask.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:22.070
Three, FAQs - we do have somewhat of an FAQ,
six.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:23.710
I'm scoring all of them.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:28.070
Then whatever those four were that were important
to me, and whatever the ones that are the

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:30.770
lowest ranking, I'm figuring out how to improve
those.

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:32.040
And I improve them.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.040
It's that simple.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:34.640
I'm doing the same thing here [outbound].

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:35.640
And I'm improving it.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:37.760
Then I get a couple ideas, then we improve.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:38.760
Again.

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:39.760
Let me do another example.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:40.760
Here's a restaurant.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:42.270
I'm running a restaurant.

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:46.710
I have a lot of friends that come to me for
advice about restaurants and they run restaurants

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:50.450
from doing a half a million a year to restaurants
doing $15 million per year.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.800
And they're always asking, "How would you
improve this.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:53.250
How would you improve that?"

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:57.340
And for me, I've been to thousands of restaurants
around the world, and I love good food.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:06:01.590
And I'm so meticulous, that I pay attention
to every single thing about restaurants, because

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:04.920
if I ever ran one, I would want it to be ran
in a certain way.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:07.330
This is what I'd be paying attention to if
I'm you.

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:08.740
Your location of your restaurant.

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:10.390
You say, "I'm not doing that well."

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:11.470
Is it even a good location?

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:14.750
I went to a restaurant the other day, yesterday
in Houston, Paul, and we're looking at the

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:15.990
sushi spot.

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:17.940
The sushi spot was all the way in the back.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:19.420
I couldn't even find this place.

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:20.960
Food was great.

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:22.430
Everything was good.

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:23.780
Horrible location.

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:30.080
If this is the main street, these were the
businesses up front, the sushi spot was here.

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:31.080
There is no street there.

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:35.640
That's a horrible, horrible location for it,
right?

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:36.640
So location.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:40.840
Where can I be found online, Yelp, on apps,
am I everywhere?

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:42.330
Parking, is parking available.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:43.940
Next, entrance, presentation.

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:46.520
I'm scoring every one of these, from 0 - 10.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:48.950
I am truly scoring every one of those zero
to 10.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:51.390
Next, my process, hostess.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:53.490
What's the script when somebody comes?

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:54.490
Who do I hire?

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:55.490
What is the attire?

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:56.490
What is she wearing?

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:57.490
What is he wearing?

00:06:57.490 --> 00:06:58.490
What's their look?

00:06:58.490 --> 00:06:59.490
What's their attitude?

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:00.490
Do I want somebody attractive?

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:01.490
What age do I want?

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:02.490
How helpful do I want them to be?

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:04.180
How do I attract how helpful they are?

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:06.170
I'm scoring this with all my hostesses.

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:10.590
If I've got five hostesses, I'm scoring every
one of them and I'm firing the bottom two,

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:11.590
okay?

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:13.660
If they're not at all like this, I'm firing
them.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:16.100
So meaning I'm hiring somebody to shop them.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.510
Let me explain what I mean by shopping them.

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:24.490
When I worked at Bally and I was selling memberships
at Bally, I used to shop all the other Bally.

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:27.110
Everybody would say, "This Bally in Chicago
is the best one!

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:28.670
This Bally in New York is the best one!"

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:29.670
I'm working at Bally.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.740
I would call that Bally.

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:33.200
I would call that Bally.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.100
Until the best guy at that Bally picked up.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.950
And I would act like I'm a customer, wanting
to buy a membership.

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:40.190
And see how he handled it.

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:42.960
I'm like, "wow, no wonder this guy's number
two in the company.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.650
No wonder this guy's number three in the company.

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:46.700
No wonder this guy's number one in the company.

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.580
He is a beast in closing on an appointment.

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:49.580
I didn't even know what to say.

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.610
He closed me, and I work at Bally."

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:53.520
I'm shopping all my hostesses.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:56.510
I'm bringing 10 people, and I'm having all
them shop them.

00:07:56.510 --> 00:08:01.220
Different personalities, single mother, single
female, a husband and wife, kids, I want a

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:05.830
whole experience, how she handles kids being
rattled and loud, I want to shop my hostesses.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:07.100
Next, ambiance.

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:08.100
What's the music?

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:09.100
Is it too loud?

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:10.100
What kind of music am I playing?

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:11.100
Is it hip hop music?

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:12.200
Is it a lounge with jazz?

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.220
Is it more salsa?

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.639
Is it more like current music that we have?

00:08:15.639 --> 00:08:18.360
Is it just, you know, the white noise music?

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:19.360
What am I playing?

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:20.360
What station am I playing here?

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:21.360
How loud is it?

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:22.360
How's the lighting?

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:25.080
How's the dress attire and the ambiance, right?

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.120
Decorations, smell.

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:27.120
Is there scent for it?

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:28.120
Is there a smell?

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:31.660
If I go into a place that smells bad, I walk
out immediately, right?

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:32.660
Service.

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:34.880
Waiter, how long it waits to come.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:36.839
For instance, I'm here, I come in.

00:08:36.839 --> 00:08:38.789
I'm timing this if I'm running a restaurant.

00:08:38.789 --> 00:08:40.309
You got to do this with your business.

00:08:40.309 --> 00:08:41.999
I walk into a restaurant.

00:08:41.999 --> 00:08:42.999
Okay.

00:08:42.999 --> 00:08:46.760
A restaurant that's empty, and it took me
six minutes to get seated, you're annoyed.

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:49.689
